+### 12.3.6 Known dependency-declaration body failures (R07-C D-M)
+
+For `env.llm_critical_deps_pinned` only, retain typed internal evidence of the
+following existing dependency-body capture failures. `DeclarationReadIssue` has
+only `unreadable` and `invalid_syntax`; `Declarations.declaration_read_issues`
+maps logical repository-relative source paths to these codes and defaults to an
+empty dictionary for legacy/manual values. It is not a persisted schema field.
+
+- For already discovered `pyproject.toml`, `Pipfile`, `environment.yml` and
+  `environment.yaml` candidates, record `unreadable` when the existing safe
+  `RepoScanner.read_text` returns None, or `invalid_syntax` when their current
+  document decoder raises its already-caught TOMLDecodeError or YAMLError.
+- For requirements roots and supported include targets actually constructed by
+  the existing bounded requirements graph, record only `unreadable`, and only
+  when the existing `is_analysis_candidate` check permits the existing
+  `read_text(source)` call and that call returns None. A missing, binary,
+  oversize, inaccessible or safely refused body can therefore be recorded.
+  A filtered node with no body-read call is not a recorded failure under this
+  section. Cache hits retain the first result without another read.
+
+Do not infer typed issues from diagnostic prose, read rejected content, add a
+read attempt, traverse another edge or expand discovery/budgets. Preserve all
+existing declarations, exact versions, lock inventory/package sets, project
+boundaries, uncertain barriers, presence results and diagnostics. Readable
+unsupported requirements lines/directives, invalid include syntax, cycles,
+depth exhaustion, unexpanded nodes, decoded wrong structures and unsupported
+entry grammar do not by themselves create either code. None of those remaining
+cases is certified by an empty failure dictionary.
+
+Keep the current canonical in-use set and package iteration. Existing qualified
+lock or exact-declaration credit wins first, followed by the existing D-F/D-S
+and D-L SKIP branches in that order. Only for a package that would otherwise
+receive the used-but-unpinned FAIL/WARNING, if the declaration failure dictionary
+is nonempty, emit one explicit SKIPPED/INFO instead. This condition is independent
+of primary-Python coverage. Do not infer a new in-use package or change the
+no-critical-package applicability skip, the empty-result Python veto or any
+other rule.
+
+The failure influence is repository-wide. Section 12.2 retains existential exact
+credit from any captured declaration, so any such failed source could conceal
+an exact declaration for any currently used, uncredited critical package. Do not
+apply the format-lock manager/nearest-project association restrictions to this
+uncertainty branch. Those restrictions remain unchanged for granting actual lock
+credit. A failed unrelated subproject or a pyproject that might only contain tool
+configuration can conservatively cause SKIP; restoring it need not reveal a pin.
+This branch grants no declaration or lock credit and does not certify completeness.
+
+Retain rule ID, aliases, category, audit level, display-name mapping and default
+finding fields. Use this exact message:
+
+```text
+{display} is used; a dependency declaration body could not be read or parsed, so missing pin evidence is not established
+```
+
+Use this exact fix hint:
+
+```text
+Review {display} declarations and failed dependency source files; restore readable, valid declaration bodies before deciding that exact pin evidence is absent.
+```
+
+Evidence first retains the current first captured declaration for that package,
+or otherwise its first captured import. Append one `kind: file` item for each
+distinct failed declaration source path in lexical order, with the exact note
+`{display} possible exact declaration unverified`; other optional evidence fields
+retain their defaults. Keep the existing final engine sort and introduce no
+aggregate outcome or per-package PASS.
+
+FAIL-only severity overrides do not promote new SKIPPED/INFO; current suppression
+still applies. An isolated WARNING or promoted CRITICAL failure can stop
+triggering exit 1. Existing D-F/D-S and D-L messages/evidence take precedence when
+several uncertainty branches apply. An independent rule WARNING can still fail
+the command; this global source-failure branch can replace every remaining
+critical-package WARNING. Default text may show Findings: PASS with a skipped
+count; default export omits skipped counts/notable warnings; complete JSON
+retains the findings. Thresholds, renderers, engine, scanner, rule IDs, schemas,
+dependencies, historical reports and five-project gold stay unchanged.
+
+This bounded body-capture policy does not settle decoded declaration structure,
+readable line/entry grammar, general include-graph failures, omitted candidates,
+unknown package use, listing, README/config/framework completeness or broader
+sufficient certificates. The whole R07-C task remains OPEN.
 
